## 2 summary (normal request → validation.outcome, code)
SQLI  GET /api/products/search?keyword=<kw>, args "keyword=<kw>": NORMAL → FAILED; elapsed ≥ threshold → TIME_BASED_DELAY → EXECUTED;
      length > baseline×multiplier → LENGTH_ANOMALY → EXECUTED; hash pattern in rows → SUCCEEDED (SqliEvaluator.evaluateNormal:46-71)
PT    GET /api/files/download?filename=<f>, args "filename=<f>": FILE_RETURNED inside upload dir → FAILED, NOT_FOUND → FAILED, ERROR → FAILED
      (running upload dir /opt/target/uploads is empty → normal download = 404 NOT_FOUND)
SSRF  GET /api/preview?url=<u>, args "url=<u>": FETCHED external → FAILED, BLOCKED (non-http/https) → FAILED, ERROR → UNKNOWN
BF    POST /api/auth/login body {"username","password"}, args "username=<u>": AUTH_SUCCESS → SUCCEEDED (CREDENTIAL_VALID), AUTH_FAIL → FAILED, DB_ERROR → UNKNOWN
      seed users: admin, user1, user2, user (data.sql)
every request to the 4 endpoints writes attack.json.log (logHttpActivity) regardless of Caldera headers.

## 4 summary (sensor alert → run linking for normal requests)
GtLogReader drops app log lines without correlation.op_id (paw) (GtLogReader readWindow) → untagged normal requests produce no AttackEvent/verdict/link.
Caldera-tagged requests: AttemptManifest.roleOf → ATTACK for any ability not in manifest (no BENIGN role).
APP_RULE links: CorrelationEngine.match RID/HEADER/UA/TIME_ONLY to AttackEvent groups only.
NIDS links: NidsCorrelator needs Caldera UA + Caldera link window for (paw, ability) + URL match to an AttackEvent.
alerts not linked to any attempt: not stored per alert; NIDS window counts only (nids_window_stat analytic - linked, orphan).
